    "title": "3 vehicle crash on I-25 sends 3 people to the hospital in Albuquerque - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jordan Honeycutt No media credit provided. ,\n3 hours ago\nALBUQUERQUE, N.M. (KRQE) – Albuquerque Fire Rescue said a three-vehicle crash on I-25 sent three people to the hospital on Wednesday. AFR said crews were sent to I-25 northbound at Lomas Blvd. just after 7 p.m. One vehicle at the crash was on its side.\nFormer Albuquerque doctor ordered to pay $1.5M restitution for role in Medicaid fraud scheme There were a total of three people; two had to be extricated from their vehicles. One patient had serious, non-life-threatening injuries. The other two had less serious, non-life-threatening injuries.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to KRQE NEWS 13 - Breaking News, Albuquerque News, New Mexico News, Weather, and Videos.",
